1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
Before it calculates, Modori asks.
When the evidence is not enough, it abstains.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Here is the payoff: a reviewable result from 649 public student records,
exported to Word locally.

3
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:30,000
I'm a social-science student. I built Modori because starting statistical work
should feel clear, not punishing.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:44,000
This walkthrough uses 649 observed records from UCI Student Performance.
Modori labels the 30-row preview before loading the full table.

5
00:00:44,000 --> 00:01:02,000
Before any method appears, I confirm what the variables mean:
study time is ordinal; final grade is scale. These decisions enter the review trail.

6
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:22,000
I ask whether study time and grades move together, then assign exact roles.
Modori asks bounded questions about independence, clustering, and weights—and records the answers.

7
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:38,000
The reviewable candidate is Spearman correlation. Its association-only boundary,
variables, missing-data policy, and experimental status remain visible.

8
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:55,000
Prepare seals the reviewed configuration but does not calculate. Only this separate
Run action produces the result: rho point two seven five, p below point zero zero one.

9
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:08,000
A second request asks for a causal effect. Modori does not substitute a convenient method.
It records that the request is outside the current scope.

10
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:31,000
During Build Week, Codex with GPT-5.6 helped turn product questions into contracts,
failing tests, implementation, and Windows verification—from variable meaning and ledger authority
to Excel recovery, safe Word export, and failure recovery.

11
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:48,000
The arithmetic and recommendation boundary are tested separately. External reference checks
support the calculation layer, while the workflow remains reviewable from data to report.

12
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:55,000
Modori asks, abstains, and waits for you to Run.
Kindness is a system behavior.
